  "slides": [
    {
      "page_title": "Pods: The Scheduling Atom",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "1. What A Pod Is",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Smallest deployable unit: one or more containers",
            "Always co-scheduled on one node, one shared lifecycle",
            "Kubernetes never schedules a bare container",
            "You scale Pods, not containers"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "2. What Gets Shared"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Namespace",
            "Shared?"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "network",
              "yes — one IP"
            ],
            [
              "IPC",
              "yes"
            ],
            [
              "PID",
              "opt-in flag"
            ],
            [
              "filesystem",
              "no — volumes only"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "shareProcessNamespace: true turns PID sharing on",
            "Containers reach each other on localhost",
            "Two containers cannot both bind port 8080",
            "pause container holds the netns open across crashes"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "3. Pods Are Mortal",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "A deleted Pod is gone — never resurrected",
            "The replacement gets a new name and a new IP",
            "Never hardcode a Pod IP. Use a Service",
            "Bare Pods are not rescheduled when the node dies"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "yaml",
          "lines": [
            "apiVersion: v1",
            "kind: Pod                # never in prod",
            "spec:",
            "  containers:",
            "  - {name: app, image: nginx:1.27}"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "sidebox",
          "title": "Mutable after creation",
          "items": [
            "image, resources (in-place resize)",
            "activeDeadlineSeconds, tolerations",
            "Everything else = replace the Pod",
            "Prod = Deployment / StatefulSet / DaemonSet / Job"
          ],
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "4. When Two Containers"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "One container per Pod is the normal case",
            "Multi-container = helpers sharing network or disk",
            "Log shipper, proxy, config reloader"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "5. Init Containers"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Run to completion, one at a time, in order",
            "All finish before any app container starts",
            "Use for migrations, waiting on deps, fetching secrets",
            "Can use a fatter image and higher privileges"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "yaml",
          "lines": [
            "readinessProbe: # may be twitchy",
            "  httpGet: {path: /ready, port: 8080}",
            "  periodSeconds: 5"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "bash",
          "lines": [
            "kubectl debug -it web-1 \\",
            "  --image=busybox --target=app"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Pods: The Scheduling Atom (cont.)",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "yaml",
          "lines": [
            "livenessProbe:  # shallow, forgiving",
            "  httpGet: {path: /healthz, port: 8080}",
            "  periodSeconds: 10",
            "  failureThreshold: 3"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "tip",
          "title": "Init failure = full stop",
          "text": "kubelet retries it per restartPolicy. Pod sits in Init:Error or Init:CrashLoopBackOff and no app container ever starts."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "6. Sidecars"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Helper alive for the whole Pod lifetime",
            "Envoy proxy, fluent-bit tailer, cloud-sql-proxy",
            "Native sidecar (1.29 GA): init + restartPolicy Always",
            "Starts first, stays up, shuts down last"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "yaml",
          "lines": [
            "initContainers:",
            "- name: logger",
            "  image: fluent-bit:3.1",
            "  restartPolicy: Always  # native sidecar",
            "  # fixes Job-never-completes"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "1. Ambassador vs Adapter",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Pattern",
            "Sidecar does"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "Ambassador",
              "proxies outbound"
            ],
            [
              "Adapter",
              "reshapes output"
            ],
            [
              "Both",
              "same mechanism"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "2. emptyDir & Start Order"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "emptyDir is the channel between containers",
            "Lives and dies with the Pod, not a restart",
            "App containers start in spec order — no ready wait",
            "Only init containers give ordering guarantees"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "yaml",
          "lines": [
            "# init: gate boot on the DB",
            "command: [sh, -c]",
            "args:",
            "- \"until nc -z db 5432; do sleep 2; done\""
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "3. Pod-Level Knobs"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "nodeSelector, affinity, topologySpreadConstraints",
            "tolerations for tainted nodes",
            "securityContext, serviceAccountName",
            "terminationGracePeriodSeconds (default 30)"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "cont": true
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Pods: The Scheduling Atom (cont.)",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "cloud",
          "title": "Don't cram",
          "text": "Unrelated services in one Pod because 'they talk' is an anti-pattern. If they scale or fail independently, separate Pods behind Services."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "4. The Five Phases"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Phase",
            "Means"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "Pending",
              "accepted, not running"
            ],
            [
              "Running",
              "bound, container up"
            ],
            [
              "Succeeded",
              "all exited 0"
            ],
            [
              "Failed",
              "one exited non-zero"
            ],
            [
              "Unknown",
              "node unreachable"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Pending = unschedulable, or still pulling the image",
            "Phase is a coarse summary, not the truth",
            "Conditions carry detail: PodScheduled, Initialized",
            "ContainersReady, Ready — Ready gates Service traffic"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "5. Container States"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "State",
            "Detail field"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "Waiting",
              "ImagePullBackOff"
            ],
            [
              "Running",
              "started, no exit"
            ],
            [
              "Terminated",
              "exitCode, OOMKilled"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "6. Restart & Backoff",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "restartPolicy is per Pod, applies to all containers",
            "Always (default, required by Deployments)",
            "OnFailure, Never — for Jobs and one-shots",
            "CrashLoopBackOff is a timer, not an error state",
            "10s, 20s, 40s … capped 5 min, reset after 10 min up"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "7. Death Sequence"
        },
        {
          "type": "diagram",
          "kind": "flow",
          "spec": {
            "nodes": [
              "Terminating",
              "drop endpoint",
              "preStop",
              "SIGTERM",
              "grace 30s",
              "SIGKILL"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Endpoint removal and SIGTERM happen in parallel",
            "In-flight requests hit a dying Pod",
            "preStop: sleep 5 is the standard workaround",
            "CMD npm start makes /bin/sh PID 1 — eats SIGTERM",
            "Use exec form, or an init like tini"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "cont": true
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Helpers, Phases & Death",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Exit",
            "Meaning"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "0",
              "clean"
            ],
            [
              "1",
              "app error"
            ],
            [
              "137",
              "128+9 SIGKILL / OOM"
            ],
            [
              "143",
              "128+15 SIGTERM"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "sidebox",
          "title": "First two commands, always",
          "items": [
            "kubectl describe pod — read the Events tail",
            "kubectl logs --previous — the dead container",
            "Every lifecycle mystery starts here"
          ],
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "1. One Job, Forever",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Keep exactly N Pods matching the selector running",
            "Level-triggered: reacts to state, not to events",
            "A missed event self-heals on the next sync",
            "A dropped message never causes permanent drift"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "diagram",
          "kind": "flow",
          "spec": {
            "nodes": [
              "list Pods by selector",
              "compare spec.replicas",
              "create or delete diff",
              "repeat forever"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "2. Three Fields"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "yaml",
          "lines": [
            "spec:",
            "  replicas: 3",
            "  selector:",
            "    matchLabels: {app: web}   # must match",
            "  template: {metadata: {labels: {app: web}}}"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Selector must match template labels or apply fails",
            "Otherwise it spawns Pods it can never see",
            "matchExpressions adds In / NotIn / Exists",
            "That set-based support is the only real gain over RC"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "3. Adoption & Ownership"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Claims any matching Pod with no controller owner",
            "Overlapping selectors across RSs are dangerous",
            "ownerReferences on the Pod point back to the RS",
            "Cascading delete garbage-collects through them"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "bash",
          "lines": [
            "kubectl delete rs my-rs \\",
            "  --cascade=orphan   # Pods live on, unowned"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_title": "ReplicaSets & The Loop",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "4. Who Dies On Scale-Down",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Pending before Running",
            "not-Ready before Ready",
            "Newer before older",
            "Higher restart count before lower",
            "Pods on nodes with more replicas first"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "sidebox",
          "title": "Bias the victim",
          "items": [
            "controller.kubernetes.io/pod-deletion-cost",
            "Annotation on the Pod, integer value",
            "Lower cost is deleted first"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "takeaway",
          "title": "Never write one by hand",
          "text": "A Deployment creates and manages ReplicaSets for you, and all the rollout logic lives one level up."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "5. Ownership Chain"
        },
        {
          "type": "diagram",
          "kind": "flow",
          "spec": {
            "nodes": [
              "Deployment",
              "ReplicaSet",
              "Pod",
              "kubelet"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "One ReplicaSet per unique Pod template",
            "Template change = new RS, old scaled down",
            "That IS the rolling update",
            "pod-template-hash added to RS selector + Pod labels",
            "So generations never claim each other's Pods"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "1. Scaling Is Not Rolling",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Changing spec.replicas creates no new ReplicaSet",
            "Only a template change makes a revision",
            "Two different operations, two different machines"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "2. Status Fields"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Field",
            "Means"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "replicas",
              "total desired"
            ],
            [
              "updatedReplicas",
              "on new template"
            ],
            [
              "readyReplicas",
              "passing readiness"
            ],
            [
              "availableReplicas",
              "ready ≥ minReadySeconds"
            ],
            [
              "unavailableReplicas",
              "the shortfall"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "3. History & Deadlines"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "revisionHistoryLimit default 10 old RSs at zero",
            "Set it to 0 and you lose rollback entirely",
            "progressDeadlineSeconds default 600",
            "No headway = Progressing=False, ProgressDeadlineExceeded",
            "It does NOT auto-rollback for you"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "bash",
          "lines": [
            "kubectl apply -f web.yaml",
            "kubectl set image deploy/web app=img:v2",
            "kubectl edit deploy/web",
            "kubectl rollout status deploy/web  # CI gate"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_title": "ReplicaSets & The Loop (cont.)",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "sidebox",
          "title": "Why deleted fields come back",
          "items": [
            "kubectl.kubernetes.io/last-applied-configuration",
            "apply computes a three-way merge from it",
            "Mixing apply with edit/patch resurrects fields",
            "Pick one path and stay on it"
          ],
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "4. Pick The Controller"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Need",
            "Use"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "stateless",
              "Deployment"
            ],
            [
              "stable identity",
              "StatefulSet"
            ],
            [
              "one per node",
              "DaemonSet"
            ],
            [
              "run to completion",
              "Job / CronJob"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Set kubernetes.io/change-cause yourself",
            "--record is deprecated",
            "It is what rollout history prints"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "5. Exactly Two Knobs"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "maxSurge and maxUnavailable, number or percent",
            "Defaults 25% / 25% of spec.replicas",
            "maxSurge rounds UP, maxUnavailable rounds DOWN",
            "Cap: total Pods ≤ replicas + maxSurge",
            "Floor: available ≥ replicas − maxUnavailable"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "6. Run The Numbers"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "replicas",
            "surge",
            "unavail",
            "cap / floor"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "10",
              "ceil 2.5 = 3",
              "floor 2.5 = 2",
              "13 / 8"
            ],
            [
              "4",
              "ceil 1 = 1",
              "floor 1 = 1",
              "5 / 3"
            ],
            [
              "2",
              "ceil .5 = 1",
              "floor .5 = 0",
              "3 / 2"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "replicas=2 is surge-only — no capacity dip at all",
            "Small Deployments feel slower but are safer",
            "maxUnavailable 0 + maxSurge 1 = zero capacity loss",
            "One new Pod at a time, needs spare cluster room"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "cont": true
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Deployments & Rollout Knobs",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "yaml",
          "lines": [
            "strategy:",
            "  type: RollingUpdate",
            "  rollingUpdate:",
            "    maxSurge: 1",
            "    maxUnavailable: 0   # safest"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "1. The Other Extreme",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "maxSurge 0 + maxUnavailable 1 = no extra capacity",
            "You run below full strength during the rollout",
            "Required under a quota or fixed license count",
            "Both zero is rejected — progress would be impossible"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "2. minReadySeconds"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "A new Pod is not available until Ready that long",
            "Continuously — any blip restarts the clock",
            "The rollout waits, so it catches ready-then-crash"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "3. The Step Loop"
        },
        {
          "type": "diagram",
          "kind": "flow",
          "spec": {
            "nodes": [
              "new RS up to surge cap",
              "wait for available",
              "old RS down to floor",
              "repeat until old = 0"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "tip",
          "title": "No readiness probe = rolling outage",
          "text": "A container counts as ready the instant it starts, so the rollout marches on while every new Pod is still booting."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "4. Pause & Resume"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "pause freezes the rollout mid-flight",
            "Further spec edits accumulate, no new ReplicaSet",
            "resume applies them all as one new revision",
            "kubectl scale still works while paused"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "bash",
          "lines": [
            "kubectl rollout pause deploy/web",
            "kubectl set image deploy/web app=img:v3",
            "kubectl set resources deploy/web --limits=...",
            "kubectl rollout resume deploy/web  # 1 revision"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Pause, Resume, Rollback",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "5. Undo Moves Forward",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "undo reverts to the previous revision",
            "--to-revision=N targets a specific one",
            "It re-applies the old template as a NEW revision",
            "History never runs backward",
            "Fast: the old RS still exists at replicas=0"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "bash",
          "lines": [
            "kubectl rollout history deploy/web --revision=3",
            "kubectl rollout undo deploy/web",
            "kubectl rollout undo deploy/web --to-revision=2"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "6. Restart, No New Image"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "rollout restart patches restartedAt into the template",
            "kubectl.kubernetes.io/restartedAt, an RFC3339 stamp",
            "Fresh rolling restart, same image",
            "How you pick up a rotated Secret or ConfigMap"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "sidebox",
          "title": "Stuck, not broken",
          "items": [
            "Failed rollouts never self-heal",
            "New Pods crashloop, old Pods keep serving",
            "Good: no outage. Bad: silently frozen",
            "Alert on ProgressDeadlineExceeded"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "cloud",
          "title": "Rollback is a lie if…",
          "text": "undo does not roll back the ConfigMap, the Secret or the DB migration it depended on. Version your ConfigMaps. And revisionHistoryLimit: 0 disables undo outright."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "1. The CI Recipe",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "bash",
          "lines": [
            "kubectl apply -f deploy.yaml",
            "kubectl rollout status deploy/web \\",
            "  --timeout=5m   # blocks until settled",
            "# non-zero exit: kubectl rollout undo deploy/web"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "2. Rolling vs Recreate"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "RollingUpdate: gradual, no downtime, 2 versions live",
            "Your app and schema must tolerate N and N+1",
            "Recreate: kill all, then start. One version, downtime",
            "For exclusive locks, breaking migrations, single-writer"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "3. Four Strategies"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "",
            "Downtime",
            "Extra cap"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "Rolling",
              "none",
              "maxSurge"
            ],
            [
              "Recreate",
              "full",
              "none"
            ],
            [
              "Blue-Green",
              "none",
              "2×"
            ],
            [
              "Canary",
              "none",
              "~1.1×"
            ]
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Pause, Resume, Rollback (cont.)",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "",
            "Versions live",
            "Rollback"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "Rolling",
              "2, mixed",
              "minutes"
            ],
            [
              "Recreate",
              "1",
              "minutes + down"
            ],
            [
              "Blue-Green",
              "2, one served",
              "instant flip"
            ],
            [
              "Canary",
              "2, weighted",
              "instant, weight 0"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "",
            "Bad build reaches"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "Rolling",
              "grows as it goes"
            ],
            [
              "Recreate",
              "100% at once"
            ],
            [
              "Blue-Green",
              "0%, then 100%"
            ],
            [
              "Canary",
              "canary share only"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "4. Doing It Vanilla"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Blue-Green: Deployments app-blue and app-green",
            "One Service, flip by patching its label selector",
            "Atomic — no in-flight version mixing"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "bash",
          "lines": [
            "kubectl patch svc app --type=merge \\",
            "  -p '{\"spec\":{\"selector\":{\"ver\":\"green\"}}}'"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Poor-man's canary: 2 Deployments, shared selector",
            "replicas 9 and 1 splits ~90/10 by Pod count",
            "That is not real weighting, just arithmetic",
            "Weighted traffic needs NGINX / Istio / HTTPRoute"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "sidebox",
          "title": "No automatic rollback",
          "items": [
            "Deployments read no metrics at all",
            "Argo Rollouts, Flagger add analysis steps",
            "They abort on error-rate or latency SLOs"
          ],
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "takeaway",
          "title": "Decision rule",
          "text": "Default RollingUpdate. Recreate when concurrency is unsafe. Blue-Green for an instant atomic revert. Canary when risk is unknown and you can measure it."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "5. Three Probes, Three Jobs"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Probe",
            "Asks",
            "On failure"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "liveness",
              "wedged?",
              "kill + restart"
            ],
            [
              "readiness",
              "send traffic?",
              "drop endpoint"
            ],
            [
              "startup",
              "booted yet?",
              "suspends the other two"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Liveness wrong = a permanent restart loop",
            "Readiness failure leaves the container running",
            "While startup fails, the other two are fully off"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "cont": true
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Strategy Matrix & Probes",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "1. Four Handlers",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Handler",
            "Passes when"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "httpGet",
              "2xx or 3xx"
            ],
            [
              "tcpSocket",
              "connection opens"
            ],
            [
              "exec",
              "exit code 0"
            ],
            [
              "grpc",
              "standard health RPC"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "exec is the expensive one — a fork every period",
            "Period 5s across 1000 Pods is real CPU burned",
            "httpGet comes from the kubelet, not via the Service",
            "It does not follow redirects; host defaults to Pod IP"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "2. Timing Fields"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Field",
            "Default"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "initialDelaySeconds",
              "0"
            ],
            [
              "periodSeconds",
              "10"
            ],
            [
              "timeoutSeconds",
              "1"
            ],
            [
              "successThreshold",
              "1"
            ],
            [
              "failureThreshold",
              "3"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "successThreshold must be 1 for liveness and startup",
            "First restart ≈ initialDelay + period × failureThreshold",
            "Compute it, do not guess",
            "Startup budget = failureThreshold × period",
            "30 × 10s = 5 min grace, then it kills the container"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "yaml",
          "lines": [
            "startupProbe:   # replaces a fat initialDelay",
            "  httpGet: {path: /healthz, port: 8080}",
            "  failureThreshold: 30",
            "  periodSeconds: 10"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Probe endpoints: unauthenticated, cheap, own port",
            "A path behind auth returns 401 = permanent failure",
            "Readiness matters at shutdown too",
            "Failing readiness is how a Pod drains before SIGTERM"
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
